      "path": "tools/bench-partial.ts",
      "content": "The snapshot still has its service worker when this navigation runs. Playwright routes do not intercept requests served by a service worker, and this project's worker serves cached `/index.html` for every navigation (`src/sw/release.ts`). Consequently `/bench-partial` can load the actual application rather than the blank document, allowing application startup to run against the copy while records are extracted and caches are removed. Bypass/block service-worker handling for the extraction context before navigating, and then unregister and verify cleanup, so preparation really reads the snapshot without running the app.",
      "existing_code": "const context = await chromium.launchPersistentContext(runProfile, { headless: true });",
      "start_line": 27,
      "end_line": 27,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "tools/bench-partial.ts",
      "content": "This labels the snapshot with the current schema version without reading its actual schema. Unlike the normal benchmark path, partial runs also skip the version-stamp check, so an older snapshot can be reported as current (or fail later when the app detects an older workspace). Read the workspace's `meta` record with key `schema` during extraction and reject unsupported/mismatched versions before writing this provenance; the current source constant is not evidence of the copied database's version.",
      "existing_code": "  schemaVersion: SCHEMA_VERSION,",
